From 43205d36537eef9acab7aa94799ab82dc38ce8d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rajesh Gugulothu <rajesh.gugulothu@amd.com>
Date: Fri, 22 Aug 2025 04:29:47 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 053/190] phy: xilinx-xhdmiphy: Add support for DPLL/MMCM clock
 primitive selection

commit 595647f8f5478b862d7a15ddea70df0e14b567fa from
https://github.com/Xilinx/linux-xlnx.git xlnx_rebase_v6.12

Versal-based cost-optimized devices have limited MMCM availability.
To address this, the HDMIPHY IP includes an option to select between
DPLL and MMCM clock primitives. This patch adds support to the driver
for selecting the appropriate clock primitive based on the IP
configuration. It enables the use of output clocks from either DPLL
or MMCM, improving compatibility with resource-constrained devices.

Signed-off-by: Rajesh Gugulothu <rajesh.gugulothu@amd.com>
Reviewed-by: Anatoliy Klymenko <anatoliy.klymenko@amd.com>
Message-ID: <1755817187-2687516-3-git-send-email-rajesh.gugulothu@amd.com>
State: pending
Signed-off-by: Quanyang Wang <quanyang.wang@windriver.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
